## What does this PR do?
Add default-off `--muon-ns-cuda-graphs` to TensorParallelMuon. Replay the existing Newton–Schulz callable without changing precision, coefficient sequence, iteration count, or update scaling. Bounded per-optimizer cache (32 graphs), same-stream workspaces, stable output ownership, eager fallback for ineligible tensors/distributed NS, and no nested capture/compile. First use checks bitwise output and unchanged CUDA RNG against eager. Reject adaptive/layer-sharded optimizer classes for this option;

## Motivation

Weight loaders copy slices of memory-mapped safetensors tensors to the GPU with `Tensor.copy_`. The source is pageable memory. On MI355X, measured inside the SGLang ROCm container:
- a pageable host-to-device copy from the page cache runs at 7-8 GB/s regardless of chunk size and torch thread count, and a strided slice (the row-parallel w2 shard of `_load_w2`) at 2.0 GB/s with one torch thread;
- a copy from pinned memory to the GPU runs at 57 GB/s;
- a single-threaded CPU memcpy from the page cache into pinned memory runs at 97 GB/s.

